data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# d002: implement greet(name), tested\\n\\n## What was delivered\\n\\n- `src/greet.py`: `greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: unittest-style tests covering a normal name\\n  (`greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`) and the empty string\\n  (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`). The test file inserts `src/` onto\\n  `sys.path` so it can `from greet import greet` without needing a\\n  package/`__init__.py`.\\n\\n## Test command and output\\n\\nRun from the repo root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n```\\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\nEXIT_STATUS=0\\n```\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nCommitted to branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`,\\ncommit `b03ae99`: \\\"Add greet(name) function with unittest coverage\\\"\\n(2 files changed, 21 insertions, on top of base `1053761`).\\n\\nNo blockers.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

